dmatest tests the idxd dmaengine workqueue
driver using the DMAEngine subsystem's dmatest module.

PARAMS to pass to the test:

required:

DMA_MODNAME:
	"idxd"
	"ptdma"
	"ioatdma"

DMA_IOMMU_CONF:
	"sm-on-lazy" (idxd only)
	"sm-on-strict" (idxd only)
	"sm-on-pt" (idxd only)
	"lazy"
	"strict"
	"pt"

optional (currently shouldn't be used with ptdma):

DMATEST_MULTITHREADS:
	int

You can find free systems using the beaker command line utility:

For system with only dsa devices:

bkr system-list --free --status=Automated --xml-filter="$(<idxd-hostreq.xml)"

For system with both dsa devices and iax devices:

bkr system-list --free --status=Automated --xml-filter="$(<iaa-hostreq.xml)"
